course: dictionary
lesson: 8238
title: Words that mean again
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are built from smaller parts, and the start of a word can change its meaning. Re- at the start of a word often means again. Rewatch is re plus watch: to watch something again.
explain: «Rewatching a favourite film is a comfort at any age; grown-ups do it too.» Rewatching means watching again, so a favourite film you watch once more brings comfort. Check it by swapping in watching again: the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «Rewatching a scary film often makes it less scary, because you know what is coming.» Rewatch can also be a noun, a rewatch: one more time watching something. You can say «It was worth a rewatch» when a film was good enough to see again.
fact: Rewatch means to watch a film, show or video again.
fact: As a noun, a rewatch is the act of watching something again.
fact: The prefix re- often means again, as in rewatch, reread and retell.
fact: Rewatching a video at school can help you notice details you missed the first time.
fact: Useful phrases: rewatch a film, on a rewatch, worth a rewatch.
exercise: «We will rewatch the science video to spot the details we missed.» What does rewatch mean here? | To buy a new video | To film a new one | To switch off the screen | *To watch again
exercise: Mum says, «Let's have a rewatch of the film tonight.» What is a rewatch? | A film that has never been shown | *A second time watching something | A kind of popcorn | A ticket for the cinema
exercise: «Rewatching a scary film often makes it less scary.» Find and copy the word that means watching again. | scary | often | *Rewatching | film
test: Sam loved the film so much that he wants to see it once more. Which phrase fits best? | Worth a wait | Worth a walk | Worth a lunch | *Worth a rewatch
test: «Rewatching a scary film often makes it less scary.» Why does this happen? | *Because you know what is coming, so you are less surprised | Because the film gets longer each time | Because the lights are always turned off | Because scary films are always boring
exam: «On a rewatch, Priya noticed a clue she had missed.» What does on a rewatch mean? | Going to the cinema with friends | *The second or later time you watch something | Watching a film on a train | Watching with the sound turned off
